/-!
# The finite Renewal Grand Tensor of a finite operational process

Paper `predictive_spectral_geometry`, labels `def:ncg-grand-tensor` and
`prop:ncg-grand-tensor-reconstruction`.

## The future-separated quotient as a concrete matrix algebra

* `exists_centralSupport`: a star-stable two-sided ideal `J` of a star subalgebra
  `A ⊆ M_n(ℂ)` is `e A` for a central projection `e ∈ J` (Hilbert–Schmidt
  orthogonal decomposition `A = J ⊕ J^⊥`).
* `exists_quotient_compression`: hence there is an isometry `V` onto the range
  of `1 - e` commuting with `A`, and compression `a ↦ Vᴴ a V` is a star
  homomorphism with kernel **exactly** `J` (`compressionHom`, `compressionHom_eq_zero_iff`):
  it realizes `A / J` concretely.

## The operational process and its Grand Tensor

* `FiniteOperationalProcess`: the finite operational input — the complete
  multitime intervention tables (multilinear functionals of the slot Choi
  matrices, at every depth `k`), the deterministic causal comb conditions on
  the reconstructed tensors (positivity, normalization, prefix compatibility),
  and the typed event grammar (branch interventions with their slots and
  Kraus vectors).
* `FiniteOperationalProcess.predictiveSystem`: the conditional event law
  `p(w | h) = p(hw)/p(h)` of the branch histories, read off the tables; the
  chain rule is proved from the comb realization (zero-probability prefixes
  propagate, `eventProb_eq_zero_of_prefix`).
* `SequentialComb.SequentialIsometricComb.histGen`: for a sequential
  realization, the branch generators pushed through the future-separated
  quotient `A^proc / N^fut` of its represented process algebra by the
  contextual future-null ideal of the causal readouts;
  `histAlgebraEquivQuotient`: `A^hist ≃ A^proc / N^fut`, letters ↦ classes.
* `GrandTensor.ofProcess`: the Grand Tensor `(A^hist, {K_r}, Z^min)` of the
  process: `system` is the process's predictive law and `gen` the quotient
  branch generators of its canonical support-minimal realization.
* `histAlgebra_realization_independent`, `grand_tensor_reconstruction_of_statistics`:
  equal complete intervention statistics (probabilities of all physical probe
  tuples) give equal predictive systems (hence `Z^min`, branch laws, updates),
  star-isomorphic represented process algebras, star-isomorphic future-separated
  history algebras compatible with every history word, equal regular traces and
  word-Gram hierarchies and equal least flat depths, for **any** choice of
  support-minimal realizations.
-/

noncomputable section

set_option linter.deprecated false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false

